            <ArticleTitle>Early emergent coronary bypass after failed angioplasty.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>385-91</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Emergency CABG for failed coronary angioplasty was required in 3.3 percent of 1,625 consecutive patients undergoing angioplasties. Twenty-six percent of the patients died in the perioperative period. Efforts must be concentrated on identifying PTCA failure prior to cardiogenic shock.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
